WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.970
Korbin: When I was investigating Hillsdale
College, I knew that WHIP was one

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.660
of the big reasons that I came in the first
place. As a student from the west coast, I

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.440
didn't know how I was supposed to split my
life between Oregon, Michigan, and now, DC,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.510
and that was actually my biggest fear going
into the program, and I found that the most

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.960
effective ways is just speak with alums. What kind of experiences have they

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:23.070
had? What did they do?
Do it for the opportunity, and I don't just

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.119
mean it in the occupational sense. You have
the opportunity to network with multiple people:

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:31.929
former congressmen, former secretaries, people
in power right now, and to really see what

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:37.079
their experiences are all about, see what
our capital's all about, see the sights, visit

00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:41.160
new places, something that a lot of people
can't do from their hometown.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.280
I think that the biggest thing that students
can do to help themselves is to reach out,

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.820
communicate with employers before-hand. LinkedIn
is a great way to do that. Just acknowledge

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:53.460
that even though on the surface an internship
might not be the most attractive option, there's

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.680
a reason that a lot of students do it, and
it's a great way to find your next career.

